# Line endings, settled once for every contributor and every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, Git falls back to each machine's core.autocrlf.
# On Windows that is `true`, which checks every text file out as CRLF. Biome — which
# this repo runs on save, in `bun run format`, and in `bun run check` — writes LF and
# has no lineEnding override (see biome.json). So the formatter rewrote CRLF files to
# LF, the byte count of every one of them changed, and Git reported 463 files as
# "modified" whose content was byte-for-byte identical to HEAD. A real 124-file change
# set was buried in 463 files of noise.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes LF canonical in the repository AND in the working tree on
# every OS, so Git and Biome now want the same bytes and neither can dirty a file the
# other just wrote. It overrides core.autocrlf, so no one has to configure anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never run end-of-line conversion or line-based diffs over these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf  binary

# SVG is text and should diff as text, but it is an asset — keep it out of language stats.
*.svg text eol=lf linguist-language=SVG

# Lockfiles are generated. Keep them LF, and keep them out of review diffs.
bun.lock text eol=lf -diff linguist-generated
